<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heraion of Samos</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Heraion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samos</a> was the great sanctuary of the goddess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hera">Hera</a> on Samos, near the mouth of the Imbrasos river, where tradition placed her birth. From the 8th century BCE it had some of the earliest monumental Greek temples, and in the 6th century the Samians began a vast temple that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> called the largest he knew. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pythagoreio">Pythagoreio</a> it is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heraion-of-samos.jpg" alt="Heraion of Samos" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tomisti · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heraion_of_Samos_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
